igured  queries  such as say prevalence information in  diseased cohorts  all of that information and more is  pre-patterned in the mastermind database  where the strength of any of these  assertions can be bolstered  by the multiplicity of different and  disparate types of  associations that um that are uncovered  through the mastermind  data so the way that janomenon  provides value to pharma clients is by  organizing all this evidence and  identifying  associations that were otherwise unknown  to our clients  or otherwise emphasizing the strength  and evidence  underpinning known associations that  drive drug discovery and drug  development  so a bit of a behind the scenes as to  how we do  this genomic interpretation at such  scale  the main takeaway here is that it's a  unique two-phasic approach  where we combine computational  intelligence  to organize and annotate and prepare  this information  for human review followed by a maximally  efficient  expedited expert curation that can be  tailored to specific disease contexts  or specific client requirements  and what results in many of those cases  an example of which i'm showing here  is a comprehensive and exhaustively  annotated compendium of information  that has been toplined uh and supported  by granular level evidence  so that the data and the information is  immediately  actionable and there's immediate walk  away insight from that accumulated  evidence  but you can also drill very deep to the  primary source of that evidence  in many cases which is to say from the  empirical literature  so i'm highlighting this example here  for a constitutional  gene in the context of  germline variants that cause cancer each  of these rows is one of those variants  with the assembled information  categorized and summarized as well as  exhaustively  curated and annotated down to the level  of individual reference citations  similarly this is an example on the  somatic side  for identifying functional variants in  the 